Ficino also aims to help those of his own calling-men of letters- to keep
their health (1 Proem 1 and 1.1). Similarly, in directing Book 2 to prolonga-
tion of life for the elderly, he focuses on what he felt to be his own age-group
("myself already old," 2.14.4, p. 520). To be precise, he had then not quite
turned fifty-six.
Ficinok ominous horoscopeb
Ficino had a very bad horoscope. I believe this accounts in part not only
