ples with the oil of violets and of water-lilies ["nenufare"] (having added to them
camphor, likewise milk and the oil of almonds and of violets). You will apply
to their noses the scent of saffron, camphor, and the peel of a sweet apple,
some vinegar in addition, but much rose-water. Strew their beds with the leaves
of cold plants. Soothe their ears with low songs and sounds. Often moisten
