friendly to light but volatile and easily dissipated. And on this account, while
it dilates itself through light as through a friend, at the same time through ex-
cess of too much light it is absolutely carried off and dissolved by great dila-
tion. Darkness, however, it flees as an enemy and therefore draws in its rays
