Chap. V I I
You will be able to foster the entire body, as we have said, and especially
the head, if you will wait to act until the planets are in Aries or each one
in his own first house. The same goes for the heart, if they are in Leo; the
stomach and the liver, if in Cancer and Sagittarius, or at least in Virgo. You
will act when those combinations occur which especially relate to the part in
question. It is also useful to know which part of the body each planet rules
in any sign whatever. You can also properly take care of each patient accord-
ing to his particular age through the four ages of the Moon. For from the new
moon to the first quarter she is youthful. Then to the full moon she is youthful
and manly. From here to the other quarter she is both manly and old. Then
to her conjunction she is old. And you will thus apply the age of the Moon
profitably to the age of the body you are treating, if you also wait until she
