through the stars as through eyes, it spreads everywhere not only its visible
but also its visual rays. By these, like a sparrow, as we have said elsewhere,'
it looks upon things below and fosters them by its look, and even thus gener-
ates them by its touch, shapes them variously, and moves them. While ex-
