With this in mind, Agriculture prepares the field and the seed for celestial
gifts and by grafting prolongs the life of the shoot and refashions it into another
and better species. The doctor, the natural philosopher, and the surgeon achieve
similar effects in our bodies in order both to strengthen our own nature and
to obtain more productively the nature of the universe. The philosopher who
knows about natural objects and stars, whom we rightly are accustomed to
call a Magus, does the very same things: he seasonably introduces the celestial
into the earthly by particular lures just as the farmer interested in grafting brings
